 "what": "The Joker's calls on 2026 weeks 1 and 2, as it really made them: the record the Pick'em Record grades for those weeks. Source, written once from git on 12 October 2026 and never regenerated by the job: betting/joker/joker.py publishes these calls for these games on every run, whatever the model in model.joblib says of them.",
 "why": "On 24 September 2026 (#118, a64ed4e) the Joker was refitted with these very games in its training (tune_2026.py, weight 0.9, chosen because it then calls them 25-7), and from 9 October the freeze at kickoff held those in-sample calls as if they had been made before the games. The owner asked on 12 October 2026 to take the retrofit out and show the record the Joker actually had. These are its real calls; the refit model still makes every call from week 3 on, before kickoff.",
 "src": {
  "published": "Week 2: the call betting/state.json carried in the last commit before the game's kickoff (`commit`, committed at `at`; `first_commit` where the same call, pick and chance, was first published in an earlier commit). Every one was made by the original Joker (model.joblib fitted 2026-09-15 19:04 UTC on 2019-2025 only, the model #117, 464fb6b, put back) and none of the 16 picks changed between then and the refit.",
  "backtest": "Week 1: the Joker did not exist before week 1 was played (its model was fitted on 15 September 2026 at 19:04 UTC, after the week's last kickoff, DEN@KC at 00:15 UTC that day; the repo begins at f0397e4 on 16 September with week 1 already graded). No call was published before kickoff, so these are the calls of that original model, fitted on 2019-2025 alone and never on 2026, on inputs built from the games before each one: out of sample, but called after the games. The state carried them unchanged from f0397e4 to 464fb6b. Counted like any other week on the Pick'em Record, as the ELO Model's own backtest weeks 1-2 are, and marked src 'backtest' on each call in the state."
 },
